    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="0671" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/2034</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the American Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">of a
                        Conversation With the Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chang Chun</hi>)<anchor n="86" xml:id="d821-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-05">February 5, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the course of a call upon the Minister for Foreign Affairs to-day I invited
                    his attention to a conversation which I had had with him on March 2,
                        1936,<anchor n="87" xml:id="d821-f2"/> at which time I had expressed the
                    hope that the Chinese Government would give further consideration to a proposal
                    of the United States for the establishment of a Sino-American Claims <pb
                        facs="0672" n="664" xml:id="pg664"/> Commission, and he had promised that
                    the Foreign Office would pursue an inquiry into various claims of which a list
                    had been furnished the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>I stated that we were still interested in this matter, and I wondered what
                    progress had been made. The Minister for Foreign Affairs promised to look into
                    this question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Trusler
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
